%T A369431 7669286,24584436,78807122,252621702,809796400,2595858574,8321204878,
%U A369431 26674199972,85506000010,274095419758,878631898608,2816515554774,9028536162646,28941599524244
%N A369431 a(n) is the number of permutations of [n] which avoid the patterns 1234, 1324, 1342, and 2413.
%H A369431 Carlo Corti, <a href="/A369431/b369431.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..400</a>
%H A369431 Carlo Corti, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21485629">OEIS A369431: Independent Maximum-Insertion Enumeration through n=22 and Formula-Derived Data through n=400</a>, Zenodo archive, 2026.
%H A369431 Permutation Pattern Avoidance Library (PermPAL), <a href="https://www.permpal.com/perms/basis/0123_0213_0231_1302/">Av(1234,1324,1342,2413), record 14688</a>.
%H A369431 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/PermutationPattern.html">Permutation Pattern</a>.
%H A369431 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Permutation_pattern">Permutation pattern</a>.
%F A369431 From _Carlo Corti_, Jul 22 2026: (Start)
%F A369431 G.f.: (1 - x)*(1 - 3*x + x^2)/(1 - 5*x + 7*x^2 - 4*x^3).
%F A369431 a(n) = 5*a(n-1) - 7*a(n-2) + 4*a(n-3) for n >= 4. (End)
%e A369431 For n = 4, the valid permutations are the 20 which are not elements of the set {1234,1324,1342,2413}, hence a(4) = 20.
%o A369431 (PARI) Vec((1 - x)*(1 - 3*x + x^2)/(1 - 5*x + 7*x^2 - 4*x^3) + O(x^31)) \\ _Carlo Corti_, Jul 22 2026
%Y A369431 Cf. A033321 (avoiding 1234, 1324, 1342), A369626 (avoiding 1234, 1324, 2413), A053617 (avoiding 1234, 1324), A165530 (avoiding 1234 and 2413).
